				<outline text="WGBH Morning Stories">
					<outline text="The Birthday Song - Deborah Henson-Conant" type="link" url="http://streams.wgbh.org/morning_stories/MS110504.mp3"/>
					<outline text="Letter from Baghdad - Charles Elias -- This week's podcast features Tony K. reading a letter from a medic in Baghdad named Charles Elias. He writes of the daily slog of his life in wartime; the conditions, his responsibilities." type="link" url="http://streams.wgbh.org/morning_stories/MS102904.mp3"/>
					<outline text="In The Buff - Erica Ferencik -- Framingham, Mass. resident Erica Ferencik takes a short walk down a very long, nude beach." type="link" url="http://streams.wgbh.org/morning_stories/MS101904.mp3"/>
					<outline text="Mother Duck - Tony Kahn -- Tony Kahn brings us a story of a devoted mother duck who led her babies down the straight and narrow path - to disaster." type="link" url="http://streams.wgbh.org/morning_stories/MS21104.mp3"/>
					<outline text="A Better Life - Fatima -- Fatima, a Brazilian immigrant to the US, longs for the warmth of home." type="link" url="http://streams.wgbh.org/morning_stories/MS31604.mp3"/>
					<outline text="Alternate Universe - E. Herberman -- Writer and scientific researcher Ethan Herberman talks about his &quot;other worldly&quot; dinners with physicist Stephen Hawking." type="link" url="http://streams.wgbh.org/morning_stories/MS32404.mp3"/>
					<outline text="My Last Nail - Don Kennington -- Poet Don Kennington, who's been shoeing horses for sixty years, drives his last nail." type="link" url="http://streams.wgbh.org/morning_stories/MS100504.mp3"/>
					</outline>
				<outline text="Reel Reviews">
					<outline text="Reel Reviews - Dazed and Confused -- Reel Review #8: Here is another fun film.  No work involved, just a good time.  Today we discuss Dazed and Confused, the 1993 film by independant film director Richard Linklater hot off his success with Slacker.  This film has a cast of young actors just about to ..." type="link" url="http://mwgblog.com/archives/2004/11/09/reel-reviews-dazed-and-confused/"/>
					<outline text="TuesdayÕs new DVDs -- Picked up three rather eclectic films today.  I got Ju-On, a Japanese horror film.  The recently released film The Grudge with Sarah Michelle Gellar is the US remake version.  I also picked up a film I saw in the theater not too long ago which was great ..." type="link" url="http://mwgblog.com/archives/2004/11/09/tuesdays-new-dvds/"/>
					<outline text="Updates - BloggerCon, Cinephile Series and more -- Audio update on my new header graphic, BloggerCon, Podcasting 101 and the Cinephile Series.  The number for Cinephile Series comments and feedback or any other audio you wish to send by phone is (267) 224-2339. Just leave a message after the beep and it will automatically get sent to ..." type="link" url="http://mwgblog.com/archives/2004/11/09/updates/"/>
					<outline text="BloggerCon Wrap Up -- First of all a big &quot;Thank You&quot; goes out to Dave Winer and everyone who worked so hard to put together BloggerCon.  It was quite an experience.  I was focused on the opportunity to interact with other podcasters so, for me, it was PodcasterCon.  I spent a ..." type="link" url="http://mwgblog.com/archives/2004/11/08/bloggercon-wrap-up/"/>
					<outline text="BloggerCon -- I had a great time at BloggerCon.  Tomorrow I'll post/podcast about it.  I want to post about so many great people I met, it will take me a day just to put all the links together. I'm not the superman blogger some of these guys are.  One ..." type="link" url="http://mwgblog.com/archives/2004/11/07/bloggercon/"/>
					<outline text="Thank you John from Dogmatic -- As you probably noticed I have a new header.  It has been provided courtesy of John over at Dogmatic. John is a Co-Director of a new media &amp; web-development company in Melbourne Austrailia. (Check out his new Texas Chainsaw Massacre theme - it rocks!) I really appreciate his generosity, ..." type="link" url="http://mwgblog.com/archives/2004/11/07/thank-you-john-from-dogmatic/"/>
					<outline text="Podcasting 101 -- I have been asked to be the presenter for two seminars entitled &quot;Podcasting 101&quot; at the Southern California Mac Fair November 13 &amp; 14. It is going to be held at Cerritos College, Student Activities Center, 11110 Alondra Blvd., Norwalk, CA   The Podcasting Seminars are at 1:30PM on ..." type="link" url="http://mwgblog.com/archives/2004/11/06/podcasting-101/"/>
					<outline text="Reel Reviews - Dr. Strangelove -- Reel Review #7: Gentleman! You can't fight in here - this is the War Room!  Dr. Strangelove - what can I say? This is a must see picture.  Yes, it is in black &amp; white - get over it!  Watch Peter Sellers, George C. Scott, Sterling Hayden ..." type="link" url="http://mwgblog.com/archives/2004/11/04/reel-review-dr-strangelove/"/>
					<outline text="Update - Cinephile Series -- Listen to the audio update for details on our movie choice for the first Cinephile Series.  The first film is Memento.  The Cinephile Series podcast will be posted in approximately 10 days.  So go out, get the film - watch it!" type="link" url="http://mwgblog.com/archives/2004/11/03/update-cinephile-series/"/>
					<outline text="Reel Reviews - Patton -- Reel Review #6: This is one of the greatest films of all time. George C. Scott excels in the role of a lifetime. Patton is one of those defining films; either you have seen it or you have not." type="link" url="http://mwgblog.com/archives/2004/11/02/reel-reviews-patton/"/>
					<outline text="Download the podcast here: Reel Reviews - Patton"/>
					<outline text="or subscribe to the Reel ..."/>
					<outline text="Direct download here."/>
					<outline text="or subscribe to the Reel ..."/>
					</outline>
				<outline text="Coverville">
					<outline text="Coverville Episode 15 -- For information on the BBC2 interviews, contact Colin Lennox at colin.lennox@bbc.co.uk. (Update 11/10; Colin is out of the office this week. Please use the following address: jacqueline.houston@bbc.co.uk) Mentioned in tonight's show: Podcat's Best of Podcasting Scott Brenner's Today's Podcast Adam..." type="link" url="http://www.coverville.com/archives/2004/11/coverville_epis_14.html"/>
					<outline text="Coverville Episode 14 -- Over a dozen episodes later, I'm starting to get this on more of a regular schedule. Sunday and Tuesday night shows will be a regular cover mix, while Thursday night shows will be a themed show. Tonight's show features music..." type="link" url="http://www.coverville.com/archives/2004/11/coverville_epis_13.html"/>
					<outline text="Coverville Episode 13: A Special All-Cover Tribute to ABBA -- Even if you don't like ABBA, you might still like tonight's show. It's all covers of ABBA songs, from Bananarama, Erasure, The Real Group, Milo Bender, Evan Dando, Information Society and a bonus track from Edelweiss. (One quick note: After..." type="link" url="http://www.coverville.com/archives/2004/11/coverville_epis_12.html"/>
					<outline text="Coverville Episode 12: The Not-So-Special Election Edition -- The votes are in, and it's...30 minutes of covers songs while you wait for election results. An election-themed opener by Bic Runga (although not a cover), and some great covers by Venus Hum, Electronic, Jon Auer, Radiohead and 10,000 Maniacs...." type="link" url="http://www.coverville.com/archives/2004/11/coverville_epis_11.html"/>
					<outline text="Coverville Episode 11: Some Halloween-inspired covers -- No MONSTER MASH. I promise. In this Halloween-inspired podcast, you'll hear some creepy, spooky -- and maybe a little ooky -- covers by the likes of Joan Osborne, The World Famous Blue Jays, Echo and the Bunnymen, Counting Crows and..." type="link" url="http://www.coverville.com/archives/2004/10/coverville_epis_2.html"/>
					<outline text="Coverville Episode 10: Some Humorous Covers -- For my tenth podcast, I delve into the funnier side of covers. You'll hear covers by Leslie Gore, Eilert Pilarm, Steve Lawrence and Edie Gourmet, Big Daddy, Bruce Springstone, The Pardon Me Boys and the Folksmen. It's good to finally..." type="link" url="http://www.coverville.com/archives/2004/10/coverville_epis_10.html"/>
					<outline text="Coverville Episode 9: Live from Corpus Christi, Texas! -- I had to wait until I found some wireless service in the Corpus Christi airport to post this show from last night. Coverville is now ASCAP legal! Details in the 'cast. Some covers by the Young Fresh Fellows, Kevin Rowland,..." type="link" url="http://www.coverville.com/archives/2004/10/coverville_epis_9.html"/>
					<outline text="Coverville Going Legal! -- I'm in the process of inking a deal with ASCAP which would allow me full license to play music from their catalog in my shows. I'll go into more detail on my show, which I''ll be recording later today. Thanks..." type="link" url="http://www.coverville.com/archives/2004/10/coverville_goin.html"/>
					<outline text="Coverville Episode 8: Live from Fairfield, California! -- By request, some Cowboy Junkies and new stuff from Paul Weller. That and a couple of &quot;Double Takes&quot; of Duran Duran's &quot;The Chauffeur&quot; and Kate Bush's &quot;Wuthering Heights&quot;. And I reveal the technical details of Coverville's production... How do I..." type="link" url="http://www.coverville.com/archives/2004/10/coverville_epis_8.html"/>
					<outline text="Coverville Episode 7: Live from gate C20 at Chicago's O'Hare Airport -- Podcasting live from a relatively empty gate during a four-hour layover in Chicago's O'Hare airport. Just a few covers - ones that I rate highly for their unique take on familiar songs. You'll hear Letters To Cleo, Kylie Minogue and..." type="link" url="http://www.coverville.com/archives/2004/10/coverville_epis_7.html"/>
					<outline text="Coverville Episode 6: Triple Takes -- A little bit different this time around. We look at different takes of two different tracks: The Ship Song (originally by Nick Cave and the Bad Seeds), and Hallelujah (originally by Leonard Cohen). You'll hopefully see the amazing differences that..." type="link" url="http://www.coverville.com/archives/2004/10/coverville_epis_6.html"/>
					<outline text="Coverville Episode 5: Live From Philadelphia! -- Live from the original home of Dick Clark's American Bandstand: Philadelphia, Pennsylvania. I put down a Cheese Steak Hoagie long enough to play some covers of the founders of rock and roll. (10/14/04: I fixed the link. I spent so..." type="link" url="http://www.coverville.com/archives/2004/10/coverville_epis_5.html"/>
					<outline text="Coverville Episode 4: &quot;A Little Bit Covers, A Little Bit Rock and Roll&quot; -- Much less of my rambling, much more music. Covers of the Hollies, Tommy Tutone, The Osmonds, The Allman Brothers, ELO, Bruce Springsteen and The Waterboys. 29 minutes |..." type="link" url="http://www.coverville.com/archives/2004/10/coverville_epis_4.html"/>
					<outline text="Coverville Episode 3: &quot;No Stinking Covers!&quot; -- I'm back from a round with the flu with a cover show that doesn't contain any covers. That's right - an entire episode of Coverville without any cover songs! This podcast is the perfect rebuttal to those who say they..." type="link" url="http://www.coverville.com/archives/2004/10/coverville_epis_3.html"/>
					<outline text="Coverville: Episode 2 -- Hopefully a little more polished. This time it's Celebrities making bad covers. William Shatner, Bill Murray, Rebecca Romijin-Stamos, Jim Carrey, Josh Ritter, Nicole Kidman, Jackie Chan and Sean Connery. How do I fit it all into one show? Listen and..." type="link" url="http://www.coverville.com/archives/2004/10/coverville_epis_1.html"/>
					</outline>
